Some of the changes in sporkhack make it harder on rogues, but there's
other changes that more than make up for it.

First go human.  I know this causes problems with hunger and poison,
but the final stats will make up for it.

Next be a neutral rogue.  This doubles your chances of getting
Magicbane, and makes it easier to handle.  This also eliminates some
of the really wimpy chaotic weapon artifact sac gifts.

Sac early and often.  While you won't have a fighting chance of
converting an altar until level 8 (and neutered alignment makes this
even harder), if you can find a neutral altar early and have a
stockpile of food then toss monsters on the barbie.  The non-artifact
gifts to look for are:

Some sort of cloak to protect against poison attacks.  (Might be
worthwhile to visit the mines).

The Helm of Vision: Human infravision plus PFSC and see invisio.
Clearly the best rogue hat and once you have it, keep a towel wrapped
around it.

Shield of Mobility: Puts the oilskin cloak to shame.

Jumping boots: Combine with Blue Dragon mail to hop through levels
quicker than greased...


